WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.269
-Progressives
of the Democratic Party

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.537
staged a collective
show of force

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.172
against the two Senate moderates
holding up

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.142
President Biden's agenda,
while Fox News and the GOP

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.144
resorted to increasingly
desperate rhetoric

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.478
to make it sound scary.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.246
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:18.251
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.420
You might recall that when it
came to getting things done,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.854
the previous president
didn't always

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:23.289
offer a reliable timeline.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.224
In fact, he even
kind of invented

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:27.527
several of his own
units of time.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.530
-I'm getting it very soon,
within a matter of weeks.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.564
That would be great
if we could go into the hospital

00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:34.000
and just cure people.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.972
And we're at a position
we're actually able to,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.273
to a certain extent,
with what we have right now,

00:00:41.273 --> 00:00:43.542
and we think,
in a very short period of time,

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.011
we'll be able to do that.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:49.115
I'll be issuing, at some point
in the not-too-distant future,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:52.285
a very strong statement on that.
-So, soon.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.486
Why say
the "not-too-distant future"

00:00:54.486 --> 00:00:55.922
when you could just say "soon."

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:59.559
Did someone set your mouth
to "Star Wars" crawl?

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.295
One of Trump's few talents
was using as many words possible

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.663
to say as little as possible.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.666
The sentences had more filler
than an Amazon package.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:10.437
"Did someone order one floss?"

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.338
Also, I love
Trump's genius insight.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.674
In the early days
of a novel coronavirus,

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.376
we didn't fully understand
that it would be great

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.879
if we could just go into
the hospital and cure people.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.614
It's like someone
brought their mom

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.716
into the "Grey's Anatomy's"
writers' room.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.884
"Just have the cure ready,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.519
and then you can focus
more on the romance.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.853
It's why we watch."

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.855
Anyway, Donald Trump
did not offer

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.425
very specific timelines
or many specifics at all.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.360
Everything he said
sounded like an FBI

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.396
recording of a Mafia phone call.
"The thing is done.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:39.966
Let's meet back at the place
in the not-too-distant future."

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.302
"Son of a bitch!
I can't do anything with this!"

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.936
But there was
one specific length of time

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.772
Trump was very fond of citing
whenever a reporter asked

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:49.776
when he would do something he'd
already promised he would do.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.944
-We're going to be announcing
something, I would say,

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:55.648
over the next, um,
two or three weeks.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.618
We've got the plan
largely completed,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.120
and we'll be filing over
the next two or three weeks.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.326
And I'll be making a big
decision on the Paris Accord

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.394
over the next two weeks.
We're gonna be having

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.196
a news conference
in about two weeks.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.999
I think you're gonna find
some very interesting items

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.502
coming to the forefront
over the next two weeks.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.903
-I think,
for a con man like Trump,

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.906
two weeks is actually
the perfect time frame

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.141
because no one remembers
anything from two weeks ago.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.042
One week, sure. But two?

00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:26.312
By the time you're done
doing the math in your head

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.248
to figure out
when two weeks ago was,

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.648
he's already stolen your wallet.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:33.486
Also, this is when I wish
"fortnight" had stuck around

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.421
as an acceptable slang
for "two weeks."

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.591
It would be great to hear a big,
dumb guy like Trump use it.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.860
"You'll be seeing
some very interesting things

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.495
over the next fortnight,

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.897
and we hope to have
an infrastructure plan for you

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.766
and fourscore and seven days,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.702
give or take --
give or take a score."

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.905
So, Trump never liked
to give a real timeline,

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.773
and when he did,
it was total bull[Bleep].

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.643
Compare that to Joe Biden,
who openly admits

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.511
that he doesn't really know
exactly

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.580
when Democrats will agree
on a path forward

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.282
for the $3.5 trillion
reconciliation bill.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.084
He just knows
they'll get it done.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.054
-President Biden trying to get
Democrats to compromise,

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.056
After a brief meeting
with House leadership,

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.658
the president seemed confident

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:14.227
that his $3.5 trillion
government overhaul

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.162
will get passed in Congress.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.731
Here you can see President Biden
arriving at Capitol Hill

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.567
to meet House leadership.
He met to try to bridge

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:25.638
the divide between moderate
and progressive Democrats.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.046
-When? When?
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:45.424
-Biden has grandpa energy,

00:03:45.424 --> 00:03:47.927
but not the kind that
gives you lots of confidence.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:51.530
You ever seen an old guy at
McDonald's say to his grandkids,

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.132
"You don't want to
get out of the ball pit,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.167
fine with me.
I can wait all day."

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.604
And you think to yourself,
"That man is going to die here."

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.039
Also, why would you say,

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.808
"six days, six weeks,
six months"?

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.108
Really? 666?

00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:06.078
What a gift to
the red-yarn conspiracy psychos

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.013
huddled in the bowels
of Facebook.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.415
Another contrast in styles

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.916
between Biden
and his predecessor

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.386
is how they handle
the outdoor press gaggle.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.454
Trump, of course,
would stand on the lawn

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:16.989
outside a whirring helicopter,

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.058
screaming like a guy
trying to talk to his date

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:22.094
at a Metallica concert.
"James gets all the attention,

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:25.865
but Lars is really the one
who holds the band together!"

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:29.201
Meanwhile, Biden goes in
for the soft-talking lean-in,

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:31.904
as he did on Saturday,
when he was asked by reporters

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.906
what it would take
to bring Democrats together.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.682
-Hey, man,
all things being equal,

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:46.418
maybe now isn't the time
for the maskless lean-in.

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.988
Even before COVID, I didn't like
when anyone got that close to me

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:52.292
during a conversation.
That's how a drunk guy at a bar

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.659
wants to let you know
he's serious.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.628
"Ha-ha-ha! I love this guy!

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.997
No, but seriously, man,
I love you.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.732
No, no, no, no, no, listen.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:04.170
You are my dawg."

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.138
Progressives
flexed their muscles

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:07.440
by withholding the votes

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.208
for the bipartisan
infrastructure deal last week

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.910
to keep the president's
larger agenda

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.479
in the form of the $3.5 trillion
reconciliation bill alive.

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:16.615
The bill would address
everything from climate change

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:18.884
to paid family leave
to childcare.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.753
It would pay for it
by taxing the rich.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.087
Polls have repeatedly shown

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:23.589
that virtually every element
in the bill is popular,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.624
and yet Sinema and Manchin
won't say

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.326
what they want or don't want.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.561
In fact, they've been so opaque
about their demands,

00:05:29.561 --> 00:05:31.530
a bunch of protesters
had to kayak out

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.166
to what Manchin calls
his houseboat to get answers.

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:35.868
-Several of
Senator Joe Manchin's

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:39.338
constituents from West Virginia
boated up to him today.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:43.175
[ Chuckles ] They paddled.
They kayaked up to the houseboat

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.411
where Senator Joe Manchin lives
when he is in Washington.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.912
Do you see him on the back
of the boat there?

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:48.747
They have boated themselves
up to him,

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.416
to the back of his houseboat,
to talk to him,

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.985
to plead with him
to get on board with the budget,

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.755
to get on board
with President Biden's agenda.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.289
-But, gang, we're working on it.
We really are.

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:59.625
We're going to continue to,
in good faith, really.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.161
We want to get a good bill
that's a balanced bill.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.797
-First of all, the "Almost"
is doing a lot of work there,

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.198
a houseboat on the Potomac,

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.201
where Manchin hangs out with
people like Lindsey Graham.

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.836 line:0%
He calls it "Almost Heaven,"

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:13.039 line:0%
but I feel like a better name
would be "Most Definitely Hell."

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.475 line:0%
Second, that's not a houseboat.
That's a yacht!

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.544
When you said "houseboat,"
I pictured something

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.713
a Florida crocodile hunter
would live in after his divorce.

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:23.148
That thing is a yacht!

00:06:23.148 --> 00:06:24.617
And it's a pretty bad sign
for democracy

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.051
that in order to get answers

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:27.186
from our
elected representatives,

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:29.187
we have to kayak out
into a river to beg them

00:06:29.187 --> 00:06:31.557
to shout answers down at us
from their giant boats.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.158
Just give us
a straight answer, Joe.

00:06:33.158 --> 00:06:36.162
At least have the same
courage of your convictions

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:39.465
as Schwartzy, the Pats fan
who told "Sunday Night Football"

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.033
Tom Brady's return
to New England last night.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:52.278
Pats fans definitely did
a few Biden lean-ins

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:54.046
at the bar last night
after the game.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.716
"Mac Jones, he's our future."

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.652
So, with the contents
of the bill being popular,

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.553
Republicans and Fox News
have had to resort

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.889
to increasingly ludicrous
rhetoric to make it sound scary,

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:06.992
like when Florida Senator
Marco Rubio tweeted last week,

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:11.364
"The $3.5 trillion Biden plan
isn't socialism, it's Marxism."

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:15.468
The bill would restore marginal
tax rates to early-2000 levels,

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:18.370
which I guess would make
George W. Bush a Marxist.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.805
Now that you mention it,

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:22.208
I do remember him
at all those anti-war protests,

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:25.278
wearing a beret
and a Che Guevara T-shirt.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.679
But, sure, paid family leave

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:30.016
and slightly higher marginal
tax rates are Marxism now.

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:32.584 line:0%
We all remember that line
from "Das Kapital,"

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:34.687 line:0%
when Marx said...

00:07:39.691 --> 00:07:41.293
What happened is,
Republicans realized

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.495
the term "socialism"
lost all meaning

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:46.198
once they screamed it about
everything they didn't like.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.899
So now they have to move on
to something else.

00:07:47.899 --> 00:07:50.369
They're like desperate parents
whose kids figured out

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.338
there's no monster
who will get them at night

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.806
if they don't brush their teeth.

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.707
"There's not a monster
in my closet."

00:07:55.707 --> 00:08:01.146
"Alright, well, a serial killer
escaped from the penitentiary,

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:03.415
and he is targeting children
who don't floss.

00:08:03.415 --> 00:08:07.619
So good luck sleeping tonight."

00:08:07.619 --> 00:08:11.156
Seems like a bunch of
the failed 2016 GOP contenders

00:08:11.156 --> 00:08:13.058
who pathetically
fell in line behind Trump

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:14.393
are now coming
out of the woodwork

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.495
to slam this bill on Sunday.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.196
Former New Jersey governor
Chris Christie

00:08:18.196 --> 00:08:21.433
for some reason is a paid
political contributor at ABC,

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:23.435
despite getting fewer votes
in the primaries

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:26.138
than cars he's stranded on
the George Washington Bridge,

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:27.472
allegedly,

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:30.409
said the old Joe Biden
was supposedly no more.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.878
-It's the death
of 2020 Joe Biden.

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:34.646
When he went to the Hill,

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:38.017
2020 Joe Biden is now
officially dead and buried.

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:40.186
The guy who ran
against the progressives,

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.554
ran against Bernie Sanders
and Elizabeth Warren,

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:45.190
ran to be a uniter
in this country,

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.526
ran saying he was
going to force compromise,

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:49.061
and he went up
to Capitol Hill

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.396
and he capitulated
to the progressives,

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:53.098
the liberals in his party.

00:08:53.098 --> 00:08:55.234
-Sure, he ran against
Bernie and Warren,

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.903
but you ran against Trump
and ended up standing behind him

00:08:57.903 --> 00:09:00.572
at every press conference
like Doody at Thunder Road.

00:09:00.572 --> 00:09:03.909
[ Chuckles ]
Fresh raff.

00:09:03.909 --> 00:09:06.445
Again, a week from today,
audiences are back,

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:09.181
and bye-bye, Doody.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:13.752
You said Trump wasn't "suited"
to be president,

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:16.255
and then you ended up following
him around like a seagull

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:18.657
chasing a potato chip
at the Jersey Shore.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.826
If 2020 Joe Biden
is officially dead and buried,

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.894
then what happened
to 2015 Chris Christie?

00:09:22.894 --> 00:09:25.163
Is he buried in the sand
on a private beach?

00:09:25.163 --> 00:09:29.301
-We do not need reality TV
in the Oval Office, everybody.

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:31.871
What's that tell you
about what we can expect

00:09:31.871 --> 00:09:36.074
if things go sideways when
you go into the Oval Office?

00:09:36.074 --> 00:09:37.843
What are you gonna do?
Just go upstairs

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:40.946
to the residence
and say, "I'm not playing"?

00:09:40.946 --> 00:09:43.416
You know, "Vladimir Putin
isn't being nice to me.

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:45.383
I'm not gonna return
his phone call.

00:09:45.383 --> 00:09:48.019
The press isn't
being nice to me.

00:09:48.019 --> 00:09:52.424
I'm not gonna hold
any more press conferences"?

00:09:52.424 --> 00:09:55.227
I mean, basically,
this is like --

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:57.329
this is like
a 13-year-old argument.

00:09:57.329 --> 00:09:59.331
-Personally, I am shocked
to look at these old clips

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:01.300
and discover that a man
as principled as Chris Christie

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.135
would change his mind
for political expediency.

00:10:04.135 --> 00:10:06.038
You know how hard we had to dig
to find these clips?

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:08.674
Our research team had to sift
through microfiche

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.642
in the basement
of 30 Rock for days,

00:10:10.642 --> 00:10:14.046
scouring dusty cans of film,
poring over old transcripts,

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:15.314
and -- What's that?

00:10:15.314 --> 00:10:16.781
These clips
are all over the Internet,

00:10:16.781 --> 00:10:19.017
and they're easy to find?
When you type "C" into Google,

00:10:19.017 --> 00:10:21.620
It autofills to Chris Christie
criticizing Donald Trump

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:25.223
before he forgave him and became
his unrequited best friend?

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:26.592
But I have to say,
probably the grossest

00:10:26.592 --> 00:10:28.394
and most detestable criticisms
of this bill

00:10:28.394 --> 00:10:30.362
have come from right-wing
media personalities

00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:32.731
complaining that if we
help people too much

00:10:32.731 --> 00:10:35.066
with things like childcare
and paid family leave,

00:10:35.066 --> 00:10:37.069
they will become
dependent on it.

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:38.904
-Senator, here's what --
here's what I fear, though.

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.974
If you tell someone,
"I'm giving you free preschool,"

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:45.044
if you tell someone, "I'm giving
you free junior college,"

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:47.913
if you tell someone, "I'm gonna
give you free school lunch,"

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:50.049
if you tell someone
"free eldercare,"

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:52.084
issues need to be addressed,
yes,

00:10:52.084 --> 00:10:53.686
but if you write
all those people a check,

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:55.955
you've got their votes.
And we're sitting there

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:58.991
and have to balance the books.
Doesn't that worry you?

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.592
-There's no work requirements.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:04.797
And in fact, Sean, there's
no education requirements.

00:11:04.797 --> 00:11:08.234
So you've got
massive welfare dependency.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:09.668
It's like the Great Society

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:12.471
to the, I don't know,
20th or 50th power.

00:11:12.471 --> 00:11:16.107
But that will damage
the soul of America.

00:11:16.107 --> 00:11:18.844
-It's a common-sense argument,
and I think you're right.

00:11:18.844 --> 00:11:20.746
One of the things that kills me
is that now that -- you know,

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:23.182
there's a free-lunch program
in New Jersey

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:26.052
and it's for everyone,
even if you you don't need help

00:11:26.052 --> 00:11:27.753
to send your child's lunch
to school.

00:11:27.753 --> 00:11:29.555
So those kids are all
gonna grow up

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:31.824
thinking, "Well, school lunch
is free," right?

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.525
And then God help the person
who comes along

00:11:33.525 --> 00:11:34.893
and tries to take that away,
Larry.

00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:36.095
-I don't know, man.

00:11:36.095 --> 00:11:38.263
When I was a kid,
they gave me a math book,

00:11:38.263 --> 00:11:40.966
and I didn't go through life
thinking books were free.

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:43.102
I'm pretty sure you learn
the difference as you get older.

00:11:43.102 --> 00:11:45.470
You don't show up to a first day
on the job and ask,

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.905
"When do you guys have recess?"

00:11:46.905 --> 00:11:50.608
A lot of stuff happens in school
that stops once school ends.

00:11:50.608 --> 00:11:53.345
You're never asked to
climb a rope in short shorts,

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.180
and you never have
to play kickball

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.783
unless you move to L.A.
I don't know.

00:11:57.783 --> 00:11:59.885
That's like 90 minutes
away from me with traffic.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:03.622
And if I'm being honest,
it sounds like it sucks.

00:12:03.622 --> 00:12:05.324
It's so revealing
what shocks these people.

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:07.793
If Congress wanted to spend
$10 trillion tomorrow

00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:10.029
to send those creepy
Boston Dynamics robots

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:11.864
to the border,
they wouldn't bat an eye.

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:13.799
But give a child
a free lunch at school,

00:12:13.799 --> 00:12:15.401
and they freak out
like their butler

00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:17.703
just mixed up the salad fork
and the oyster fork.

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:19.304
I wouldn't be surprised
if they said,

00:12:19.304 --> 00:12:20.939
"They can have their free lunch

00:12:20.939 --> 00:12:24.509
if they can get
by the Boston Dynamics robot,"

00:12:24.509 --> 00:12:25.578
which I don't think
is that hard.

00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:27.146
I think you just play,
"Do You Love Me,"

00:12:27.146 --> 00:12:28.981
and they have to dance.

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:31.483
"You must pass me
to receive your tater tots."

00:12:31.483 --> 00:12:32.818
[ "Do You Love Me" plays ]

00:12:32.818 --> 00:12:33.886
-♪ Do you love me?"

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:35.454
-♪ I can really move ♪

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.189
-"No, no, no, no."

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:38.691
-♪ I'm in the groove ♪

00:12:38.691 --> 00:12:40.292
-♪ Now, do you love me? ♪

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:44.263
[ Laughter ]

00:12:44.263 --> 00:12:45.464
-How much did that song cost?

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:49.969
Oh, that was a --
That was a mistake.

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:51.670
The progressives
in the Democratic Party

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.538
finally flexed their muscles
and showed

00:12:53.538 --> 00:12:55.040
that the corporate-backed
centrists

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.341
don't get to call all the shots.

00:12:56.341 --> 00:12:58.444
The things they're asking for
are already compromises.

00:12:58.444 --> 00:12:59.745
There are things
that should be automatic

00:12:59.745 --> 00:13:01.046
in a decent, humane society,

00:13:01.046 --> 00:13:03.381
like dental coverage for seniors
or paid family leave,

00:13:03.381 --> 00:13:05.384
not to mention
the massive urgency

00:13:05.384 --> 00:13:06.752
of tackling climate change.

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:08.186
Meanwhile, Republicans
at Fox News

00:13:08.186 --> 00:13:10.121
are losing their minds
and acting like helping people

00:13:10.121 --> 00:13:12.958
pay for childcare
is some kind of sci-fi dystopia

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:14.993
set in the...
-Not-too-distant future.

00:13:14.993 --> 00:13:17.128
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:17.128 --> 00:13:20.533
[ Theme music plays ]

00:13:20.533 --> 00:13:21.666
God's Love We Deliver cooks

00:13:21.666 --> 00:13:23.402
and brings over 2 million
meals a year

00:13:23.402 --> 00:13:25.537
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:13:25.537 --> 00:13:27.172
cancer, and other
serious illnesses,

00:13:27.172 --> 00:13:28.673
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:13:28.673 --> 00:13:30.976
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.579
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

